      "note": [
        "The statistics refers to areas that were valid (i.e. had gained legal force) on the December 31 reference year.",
        "Formally protected nature in this table includes the instruments national parks, nature reserves, nature conservation areas, habitat protection areas (in forest and and other type of nature), Natura 2000 (all areas), nature conservation agreements and intra-governmental agreements.",
        "Share in percent of total area by type of nature.",
        "Due to a change in methodology, values for the habitat types 'Lakes and watercourses', 'Open wetlands' have been revised regarding 2021.",
        "The source of data on nature types types and forest land is the Swedish Environmental Protection Agency’s National Land Cover Database (NMD). The statistics are calculated based on the latest available version of NMD for the reference year. Statistics for 2018 and 2019 use NMD2018 v1.0 as the source. Statistics for 2020–2024 use NMD2018 v1.1 as the source. Statistics for 2025 onwards use NMD2023 v2.1 as the source.",
        "Exclusive economic zone (EEZ)\r\nA zone outside Sweden´s territorial border. The zone is measured as the surface of the sea. \r\nSome marine Natura 2000 areas are located outside Sweden´s territorial border and the EEZ but are in fact small marginal parts of larger marine Natura 2000 areas located in the EEZ. These areas are the result of differences in data quality and scales. The areas are included in statistics at national level, but not at county level. "
      ],
